#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "2de283b3-992c-588c-8bda-e880779fa264" :question/math-academy-id "e-5796" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/658fa5a494ef01b5924847335ce863aa8c6b5f8adee5ee97967a8c8bebd83a80.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x_1=-2},$ ${x_2=3},$ and ${x_{3,4}=1 \\pm 3\\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is ${a=1}.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (x-(-2))(x-(3))(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x+2)(x-3)(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)(x-3)(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-3x+2x-6)({x}^{2}-x(1-3\\text{i})-x(1+3\\text{i})+(1+3\\text{i})(1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-x-6)({x}^{2}-2x+10) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+10{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-10x-6{x}^{2}+12x-60 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+2x-60 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^4 - 3x^3 + 6x^2 + 2x - 60.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087587 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Four Real Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "3630f36c-b507-5540-bb11-aeda6aa4d656" :question/math-academy-id "e-8801" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=0, x_2=-1,x_3=2$ and $x_4=-3,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $4.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x_1=0, x_2=-1},$ ${x_3=2},$ and ${x_4=-3},$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is ${a=4},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =4(x-0)(x-(-1))(x-2)(x-(-3)) \\\\  & =4(x-0)(x+1)(x-2)(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-0)(x+1)(x-2)(x+3) & =4({x}^{2}+x)({x}^{2}+x-6) \\\\  & =4({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-6x) \\\\  & =4({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}-6x) \\\\  & =4{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}-24x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 4x^4+8x^3-20x^2-24x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Four Real Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50f75880-5423-5413-91cf-8905c8b404ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}+64x+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352807} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7b0f52-436d-5620-8460-1342248586c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-64x+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352808} {:answer/id #uuid "f40449d6-6900-5f7f-8606-4009e8670601" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-64x+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352809} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b15e4e-f853-5223-920e-547d6175fb2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352810} {:answer/id #uuid "c75a1e97-739a-5760-b690-f6e54434ef3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+10{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}+64x+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5b15e4e-f853-5223-920e-547d6175fb2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352810} :answer-field/id #uuid "344bf595-272b-5b00-933f-9c597371a388" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "278ce71d-00cf-5c20-9289-38eadcd1be8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105748" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=2,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=2,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =2(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x-2) & =2({x}^{2}-4x+4)({x}^{2}-4x+4) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}+16{x}^{2}-16x+4{x}^{2}-16x+16) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-32x+16) \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Four Real Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9422069-f2b7-5e56-8646-56eae72b341f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}+24x-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352814} {:answer/id #uuid "78cab7f7-1ae2-5578-8c97-a1e8664e49a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352815} {:answer/id #uuid "b26e71eb-8845-5d6b-8c9a-4b6b60874a28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+5{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+12x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352816} {:answer/id #uuid "642df560-da71-590c-a8d2-4ee7a0b90265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+8x-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352817} {:answer/id #uuid "d255d045-ef7c-59ed-8133-f6358d42c9eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+6x-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78cab7f7-1ae2-5578-8c97-a1e8664e49a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352815} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2023096-467d-5dde-b600-395eae870341" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66a0bb88-71dc-5b62-903b-60d272d88560" :question/math-academy-id "q-107795" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1,{x}_{2}=2,{x}_{3}=-4$ and ${x}_{4}=4$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1,{x}_{2}=2,$ ${x}_{3}=-4,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-1)(x-2)(x-(-4))(x-4) \\\\  & =(x-1)(x-2)(x+4)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)(x-2)(x+4)(x-4) & =({x}^{2}-3x+2)({x}^{2}-16) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-16{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3}+48x+2{x}^{2}-32 \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f17c198-f797-5db0-b6c5-784e2f9431f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^4+6x^3+18x^2-54x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352821} {:answer/id #uuid "08c2cd94-45b2-5f67-acad-7ee02acd2f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^4+6x^3+18x^2+54x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08c2cd94-45b2-5f67-acad-7ee02acd2f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^4+6x^3+18x^2+54x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352822} :answer-field/id #uuid "581a2041-b571-5130-b013-20e48f898225" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76ebd207-119e-52cd-b4d5-03e4755976db" :question/math-academy-id "q-275317" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/431ba020bfc39615e1d49a866c6ee7c30cf8cc8f84ebde6866ef0e0cb9c8708b.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,81$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{1}=1,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-3))(x-1)(x-(-3\\text{i}))(x-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x-1)(x+3\\text{i})(x-3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+3)(x-1)(x+3\\text{i})(x-3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}-x+3x-3)({x}^{2}-3\\text{i}x+3\\text{i}x-(3\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+2x-3)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+9{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3}+18x-3{x}^{2}-27) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+18x-27) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{4}+6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}+54x-81 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}+54x\\,-81.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Four Real Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158c8e1e-fd39-57da-a0e6-1f7666a5b978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^4+x^3-18x^2+52x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352825} {:answer/id #uuid "231a6c66-6af6-5e0a-a5a3-f3e49b84564f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^4+x^3-18x^2-52x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "231a6c66-6af6-5e0a-a5a3-f3e49b84564f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^4+x^3-18x^2-52x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352826} :answer-field/id #uuid "8add5f23-ddad-5b5a-b410-78fbba64bbe8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5cee7fe-1c83-5fa8-92d1-eceb09bbcaf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-319369" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and ${x}_{4}=5$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,40$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and ${x}_{4}=5,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+2)(x+2)(x+2)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)(x+2)(x+2)(x-5) & =({x}^{2}+4x+4)({x}^{2}-3x-10) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-40x+4{x}^{2}-12x-40 \\\\  & ={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}-52x-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}-52x-40.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Four Real Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d4dfac-ca77-5d5e-aa0b-879bd902e88f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^4-12x^2-16x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18d4dfac-ca77-5d5e-aa0b-879bd902e88f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^4-12x^2-16x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352829} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fd529b3-9c60-5e22-8225-34f7d41c3a99" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9516825-da50-5582-90ed-716cd564fd9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-319377" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-1,$ and ${x}_{4}=3$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,6$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-1,$ and ${x}_{4}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =2(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-3) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x+1)(x+1)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x+1)(x+1)(x-3) & =2({x}^{2}+2x+1)({x}^{2}-2x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-6x+{x}^{2}-2x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-0{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-8x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}-12{x}^{2}-16x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{4}-12{x}^{2}-16x-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Four Real Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e4928f5-aff4-569f-99c7-91a38ac66f00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x^4+36x^3-108x^2-576x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e4928f5-aff4-569f-99c7-91a38ac66f00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9x^4+36x^3-108x^2-576x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352832} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fb52441-f7d4-5050-a525-a1939bb526d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d28d5124-469a-5f65-a3be-7cbfc59abf13" :question/math-academy-id "q-319949" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2,$ ${x}_{3}=-4,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $9.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,576$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2,$ ${x}_{3}=-4,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=9,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =9(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-(-4))(x-4) \\\\  & =9(x+2)(x+2)(x+4)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x+2)(x+2)(x+4)(x-4) & =9({x}^{2}+4x+4)({x}^{2}-16) \\\\  & =9({x}^{4}-16{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-64x+4{x}^{2}-64) \\\\  & =9({x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-64x-64) \\\\  & =9{x}^{4}+36{x}^{3}-108{x}^{2}-576x-576.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=9{x}^{4}+36{x}^{3}-108{x}^{2}-576x-576.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b61e801d-c689-5e03-a1f7-ea427a430255" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^4-21x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352835} {:answer/id #uuid "24a51abe-b716-5c14-b918-1bd85f0bcaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^4+21x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24a51abe-b716-5c14-b918-1bd85f0bcaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^4+21x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352836} :answer-field/id #uuid "669d6088-8a14-5435-8756-3e848a70ff16" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "021b26bc-0ff0-575c-a6e8-6605470c927a" :question/math-academy-id "q-320074" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/fb8d76e5fb2e83676fbab4178b523bf8cbff076490f12fa8be17c37ce06e1820.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,100$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 2,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 5\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1(x-2)(x-(-2))(x-5\\text{i})(x-(-5\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x+2)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x+2)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x-2x-4)({x}^{2}+5\\text{i}x-5\\text{i}x-(5\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4)({x}^{2}+25) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+25{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-100 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}-100 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}-100.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "070f6cda-b78c-5c39-865d-d6cec8d18555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^4-6x^3+18x^2-24x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "070f6cda-b78c-5c39-865d-d6cec8d18555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^4-6x^3+18x^2-24x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352839} :answer-field/id #uuid "46d227b6-12ef-52ca-951f-3033e6d3d9a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "201097fd-4f47-5897-ac43-904b3aaad274" :question/math-academy-id "q-320292" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/4eafeae1c77e3e75cb2b281181346eeb7e96ca5e1bd15ec11d722109469557a1.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,24$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 2\\text{i}$  and ${x}_{3,4}=1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+2\\text{i}x-2\\text{i}x-(2\\text{i})^{2})({x}^{2}-x(1-\\text{i})-x(1+\\text{i})+(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4)({x}^{2}-2x+2) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}-8x+8) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-8x+8) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x+24 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x+24\\,.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7df4e54-eb56-5909-9eac-4132f178cc7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} - 3x^{3} - 12x - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087001} {:answer/id #uuid "d55caf15-5c98-5438-bb19-57d0c4e4f9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} - 3x^{3} + 10x^{2} - 2x - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087002} {:answer/id #uuid "0f50a137-98fe-5444-b7e3-1ecaf71c4e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} + 3x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 2x - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087003} {:answer/id #uuid "35049fed-867c-57a5-81d4-ffa314df0c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} + 10x^{2} - 2x - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087004} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7debf4-ad8d-5d41-a200-fa1737426947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} - 3x^{3} - 5x^{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7df4e54-eb56-5909-9eac-4132f178cc7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} - 3x^{3} - 12x - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087001} :answer-field/id #uuid "879680ad-cc40-5554-b250-0c5b6fba0a88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c0ee8e9-ffd1-5c4b-8b1a-28665a076edc" :question/math-academy-id "q-8210" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/07724ed5ffd4843ab0a23b0029eeec6291ae698aba71f56f99fb7ac565287932.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1(x-(-1))(x-4)(x-(-2\\text{i}))(x-(2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =1(x+1)(x-4)(x+2\\text{i})(x-2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x-4)(x+2\\text{i})(x-2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+x-4x-4)({x}^{2}+(2\\text{i}-2\\text{i})x-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-3x-4)({x}^{2}+4) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3}-12x-4{x}^{2}-16 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186352840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quartic Polynomial Given Two Real and Two Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da7f375d-61e9-5eb5-ab3c-4b027c7b7dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+3{x}^{2}+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352842} {:answer/id #uuid "1cbcd896-a837-5678-9c92-e45ea292b9b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}+7x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352843} {:answer/id #uuid "159a62f5-39ca-5f8d-974d-981cfa7554b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352844} {:answer/id #uuid "25c4b2c1-c852-5e0e-9b5c-8ef4a57c8c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352845} {:answer/id #uuid "3342da64-005d-5559-927a-80dddda95487" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25c4b2c1-c852-5e0e-9b5c-8ef4a57c8c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352845} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d2365c6-7ed9-53c3-8401-f58ce710439a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b8c31ed-b430-578b-beff-5b3dbca10d94" :question/math-academy-id "q-8212" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/8fb9e432fe79c363a42d362ef5c352eab6e8b55b83583f2a946ed9251ce293e3.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 1,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1(x-1)(x-(-1))(x-(4\\text{i}))(x-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =1(x-1)(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)(x+1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+x-x-{1}^{2})({x}^{2}+4\\text{i}x-4\\text{i}x-(4\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-1)({x}^{2}+16) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+16{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-16 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{4}+15{x}^{2}-16.$"}]}
